{
  "schema": 1,
  "about": "Stage art <-> sim geometry (ST-4). Written by tools/art/stages/build_stages.py; do not hand-edit.",
  "conventions": {
    "px": "illustration pixels, origin top-left of Full.png / Backdrop.png, y down",
    "milli": "world milli-units (1000 = 1 unit), x right, y up; (0,0) = centre of MAIN's walkable top = sim feet-relative milli (MAIN top = 0)",
    "pxToMilli": "xMilli = round((xPx - originPx[0]) * 1000 / pxPerUnit); yMilli = round((originPx[1] - yPx) * 1000 / pxPerUnit)",
    "platform": "topPx/topMilli = walkable top (first ink row of the slab); left/right = outer edge of the slab outline; cxMilli/topMilli/halfWMilli feed ChibiPlatform(cx, top, halfW)",
    "sprite": "Resources.Load<Sprite>(file) is imported with pixelsPerUnit = ppu and a custom pivot (pivotNorm, bottom-left normalized). Place the transform at worldMilli / 1000 with scale 1 (parallax layers: scale = 'scale') and the art lands exactly on the colliders. Moving platforms: worldMilli is the art (home) position; the view adds the sim's offset."
  },
